---TcpRoute is the resource defining how TCP traffic should be routed by a Mesh/Gateway resource.
---@class gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRoute
---@field selfLink? string Output only. Server-defined URL of this resource
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the resource was updated.
---@field name? string Identifier. Name of the TcpRoute resource. It matches pattern `projects/*/locations/*/tcpRoutes/tcp_route_name>`.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the resource was created.
---@field labels? gcp.networkservices_v1.StringMap Optional. Set of label tags associated with the TcpRoute resource.
---@field rules? gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteRuleList Required. Rules that define how traffic is routed and handled. At least one RouteRule must be supplied. If there are multiple rules then the action taken will be the first rule to match.
---@field gateways? gcp.networkservices_v1.StringList Optional. Gateways defines a list of gateways this TcpRoute is attached to, as one of the routing rules to route the requests served by the gateway. Each gateway reference should match the pattern: `projects/*/locations/*/gateways/`
---@field meshes? gcp.networkservices_v1.StringList Optional. Meshes defines a list of meshes this TcpRoute is attached to, as one of the routing rules to route the requests served by the mesh. Each mesh reference should match the pattern: `projects/*/locations/*/meshes/` The attached Mesh should be of a type SIDECAR
---@field description? string Optional. A free-text description of the resource. Max length 1024 characters.

---@alias gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteList gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRoute[]

---The specifications for routing traffic and applying associated policies.
---@class gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteAction
---@field destinations? gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteDestinationList Optional. The destination services to which traffic should be forwarded. At least one destination service is required. Only one of route destination or original destination can be set.
---@field originalDestination? boolean Optional. If true, Router will use the destination IP and port of the original connection as the destination of the request. Default is false. Only one of route destinations or original destination can be set.
---@field idleTimeout? string Optional. Specifies the idle timeout for the selected route. The idle timeout is defined as the period in which there are no bytes sent or received on either the upstream or downstream connection. If not set, the default idle timeout is 30 seconds. If set to 0s, the timeout will be disabled.

---Describe the destination for traffic to be routed to.
---@class gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteDestination
---@field serviceName? string Required. The URL of a BackendService to route traffic to.
---@field weight? number Optional. Specifies the proportion of requests forwarded to the backend referenced by the serviceName field. This is computed as: - weight/Sum(weights in this destination list). For non-zero values, there may be some epsilon from the exact proportion defined here depending on the precision an implementation supports. If only one serviceName is specified and it has a weight greater than 0, 100% of the traffic is forwarded to that backend. If weights are specified for any one service name, they need to be specified for all of them. If weights are unspecified for all services, then, traffic is distributed in equal proportions to all of them.

---@alias gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteDestinationList gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteDestination[]

---RouteMatch defines the predicate used to match requests to a given action. Multiple match types are "OR"ed for evaluation. If no routeMatch field is specified, this rule will unconditionally match traffic.
---@class gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteMatch
---@field address? string Required. Must be specified in the CIDR range format. A CIDR range consists of an IP Address and a prefix length to construct the subnet mask. By default, the prefix length is 32 (i.e. matches a single IP address). Only IPV4 addresses are supported. Examples: "10.0.0.1" - matches against this exact IP address. "10.0.0.0/8" - matches against any IP address within the 10.0.0.0 subnet and 255.255.255.0 mask. "0.0.0.0/0" - matches against any IP address'.
---@field port? string Required. Specifies the destination port to match against.

---@alias gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteMatchList gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteMatch[]

---Specifies how to match traffic and how to route traffic when traffic is matched.
---@class gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteRule
---@field matches? gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteMatchList Optional. RouteMatch defines the predicate used to match requests to a given action. Multiple match types are "OR"ed for evaluation. If no routeMatch field is specified, this rule will unconditionally match traffic.
---@field action? gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteAction Required. The detailed rule defining how to route matched traffic.

---@alias gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteRuleList gcp.networkservices_v1.TcpRouteRouteRule[]

